# Animation clock

Before changing morph playback, timers, live preview, titles, settings preview, or `whenAttached`, read `docs/animation-clock.md` and follow it.

- Schedule morph timeouts, frames, and visibility only through `src/animation-clock.ts`.
- Do not call `setTimeout`, `requestAnimationFrame`, or `IntersectionObserver` on a morph, and do not cache `window` from `createMorph` time.
- The settings preview must keep animating when the editor window is covered. That is the regression check.

```typescript
// BAD — window captured while the element is still in the editor
const clock = window;
clock.requestAnimationFrame(step);

// GOOD — window read when the frame is requested, after append
requestElementFrame(el, step);
```
